     "code": "\"\"\"\nCODE OBJECTS (PyCodeObject)\n=============================\n\nA code object represents a compiled block of Python code.\nIt contains the bytecode and metadata needed for execution.\n\nCreated by:\n  - Compiling functions, classes, modules, lambdas, comprehensions\n  - compile() built-in\n\nKey Attributes:\n  co_code        → bytecode instructions (bytes)\n  co_consts      → tuple of constants used\n  co_names       → tuple of names used (global variables, attributes)\n  co_varnames    → tuple of local variable names\n  co_freevars    → tuple of free variables (from enclosing scope)\n  co_cellvars    → tuple of cell variables (captured by inner functions)\n  co_argcount    → number of positional arguments\n  co_filename    → source file name\n  co_firstlineno → first line number\n  co_stacksize   → maximum stack depth needed\n  co_flags       → compiler flags\n\nCode objects are:\n  - Immutable\n  - Created at compile time (not runtime)\n  - Shared between function instances\n  - Stored as constants in outer code objects\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef demo_code_objects():\n    \"\"\"Inspect code objects.\"\"\"\n    def greet(name, greeting=\"Hello\"):\n        message = f\"{greeting}, {name}!\"\n        return message\n\n    code = greet.__code__\n    print(f\"  Type: {type(code)}\")\n    print(f\"  co_argcount: {code.co_argcount}\")\n    print(f\"  co_varnames: {code.co_varnames}\")\n    print(f\"  co_consts: {code.co_consts}\")\n    print(f\"  co_names: {code.co_names}\")\n    print(f\"  co_stacksize: {code.co_stacksize}\")\n    print(f\"  co_filename: {code.co_filename}\")\n    print(f\"  co_firstlineno: {code.co_firstlineno}\")\n    print(f\"  co_flags: {code.co_flags}\")\n    print(f\"  co_code (first 20 bytes): {code.co_code[:20]}\")\n\n\nprint(\"Q132: Code Objects\")\ndemo_code_objects()\nprint()",
