     "t": "code",
     "lang": "python",
     "code": "\"\"\"\nGENERATOR INTERNALS\n=====================\n\nA generator is a function that uses 'yield' and returns a generator object.\n\nHow it works:\n  1. Calling a generator function does NOT execute the body\n  2. It creates a generator object that wraps a frame object\n  3. The frame is \"suspended\" — it keeps all local state\n  4. Each next() call resumes execution until the next yield\n  5. yield suspends the frame and returns the value\n  6. Frame state is fully preserved between calls\n\nGenerator Object Structure:\n  gi_frame    → suspended frame object (None after exhaustion)\n  gi_code     → code object\n  gi_running  → True while generator is executing\n  gi_yieldfrom → object being iterated by 'yield from'\n\nBytecode:\n  - yield compiles to YIELD_VALUE instruction\n  - Generator functions have CO_GENERATOR flag in co_flags\n\nState machine:\n  GEN_CREATED   → just created, not yet started\n  GEN_RUNNING   → currently executing (between send/next and yield)\n  GEN_SUSPENDED → waiting at a yield point\n  GEN_CLOSED    → completed or closed\n\nMethods:\n  __next__()    → resume execution, get next value\n  send(value)   → resume and send value INTO generator\n  throw(exc)    → throw exception at yield point\n  close()       → throw GeneratorExit, finalize\n\"\"\"\n\n\ndef demo_generator_internals():\n    \"\"\"Inspect generator objects.\"\"\"\n    def counter(start, end):\n        \"\"\"Simple counter generator.\"\"\"\n        current = start\n        while current < end:\n            yield current\n            current += 1\n\n    gen = counter(1, 5)\n\n    # Generator object attributes\n    print(f\"  Type: {type(gen)}\")\n    print(f\"  gi_code: {gen.gi_code}\")\n    print(f\"  gi_frame: {gen.gi_frame}\")\n    print(f\"  gi_running: {gen.gi_running}\")\n\n    # Frame preserved between yields\n    print(f\"\\n  next(gen) = {next(gen)}\")\n    print(f\"  Frame locals: {gen.gi_frame.f_locals}\")\n    print(f\"  next(gen) = {next(gen)}\")\n    print(f\"  Frame locals: {gen.gi_frame.f_locals}\")\n\n    # After exhaustion\n    for _ in gen:\n        pass\n    print(f\"\\n  After exhaustion, gi_frame = {gen.gi_frame}\")\n\n    # Generator function has CO_GENERATOR flag\n    print(f\"  CO_GENERATOR flag: {bool(counter.__code__.co_flags & 0x20)}\")\n\n    # Disassembly shows YIELD_VALUE\n    print(\"\\n  Bytecode (showing yield):\")\n    dis.dis(counter)\n\n\nprint(\"Q144: Generator Internals\")\ndemo_generator_internals()\nprint()",
